From fad72a793c0afdf1557dd8ce42daeaf7d5e3f706 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:49:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 076/100] script: resizeScreen, engine.screenResolution and
 cursorScreenPosition from the host's screen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

wp_project_hint_size (the host's output size) now reaches a scene: it is the screen the scene
shows on. engine.screenResolution reads it ("Screen resolution in pixels"; it was the scene's
own size, which it stays until a host hints one), and a change after the scene is up sends
resizeScreen (size) to every script at the next tick — WE: "called every time the wallpaper
resizes because of a change to the current screen resolution", and "NOT called automatically
when the wallpaper is first created" (lib.sceneScript.d.ts 2.8), so a size hinted before the
first frame is the screen from the start, with no event. 3042492564 recomputes its scale there.

IInput.cursorScreenPosition is "the cursor on the screen in pixels" (d.ts); it was 0..1. It is
now the pointer in screenResolution's pixels, the scene covering the screen (scaled to cover,
centred): 3509243656 centres the cursor with screenResolution / 2. Inferred: the cover mapping
(the host's) and y down (Windows' screen coordinates).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md F8; IInput.cursorScreenPosition
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
